-- --> <!-- -->of <!-- -->37<!-- --> · <!-- -->16<!-- --> in <!-- -->the past year</p></div><ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../ssh">#<!-- -->ssh</a></li><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../security">#<!-- -->security</a></li><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../linux">#<!-- -->linux</a></li></ul></header><div data-slot="alert" role="note" class="group/alert relative grid w-full gap-0.5 rounded-lg border text-left text-sm has-data-[slot=alert-action]:relative has-data-[slot=alert-action]:pr-18 has-[&gt;svg]:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] has-[&gt;svg]:gap-x-2 *:[svg]:row-span-2 *:[svg]:translate-y-0.5 *:[svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 text-card-foreground mb-10 max-w-3xl border-tint-ochre/30 bg-tint-ochre/10 px-4 py-3 *:[svg]:text-tint-ochre"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-rotate-ccw-clock lucide-history" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8"/><path d="M3 3v5h5"/><path d="M12 7v5l4 2"/></svg><div data-slot="alert-title" class="font-medium group-has-[&gt;svg]/alert:col-start-2 [&amp;_a]:underline [&amp;_a]:underline-offset-3 [&amp;_a]:hover:text-foreground">This article is out of date</div><div data-slot="alert-description" class="text-sm text-balance md:text-pretty [&amp;_a]:underline [&amp;_a]:underline-offset-3 [&amp;_a]:hover:text-foreground [&amp;_p:not(:last-child)]:mb-4 text-foreground">Written in 2015. Versions, APIs and advice may have changed since.</div></div><article class="prose-ui w-full max-w-3xl pb-10"><p>SSH is a must have tool for every System administrator or DevOps Engineer. It provides you a secure way to access remote servers. But, if you use standard password authentication there is always a chance that someone will break into system due to weak password. This potential risk increases if multiple users have SSH access to the server, because system administrator can’t influence to the users to make a better passwords.</p>
<p>Contents</p>
<ul>
<li>1 The Idea Of Public Key Cryptography</li>
<li>2 Generate Keys</li>
<li>3 Transfer The Public Key To The Server</li>
<li>4 Disable Password Authentication</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="the-idea-of-public-key-cryptography">The Idea Of Public Key Cryptography</h2>
<p>The basic idea behind key-based SSH authentication rely on <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public-key_cryptography" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="asymmetric cryptography">asymmetric cryptography</a> also know as <em>public key cryptography</em>. This type of cryptographic algorithm require two separate keys. The first key is a <em><strong>secret</strong></em> or <em><strong>private</strong></em> key, and second is a <em><strong>public</strong></em> key. Public key is used to encrypt <em>plaintext,</em> whereas private key is used to decrypt <em>ciphertext</em>. You can learn more about public-key cryptography in <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20150306041524/https://developer.mozilla.org/en/docs/Introduction_to_Public-Key_Cryptography" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Introduction to Public-Key Cryptography">this</a> MDN (Mozilla Developer Network) article.</p>
<h2 id="generate-keys">Generate Keys</h2>
<p>First what you need to do on the client machine is to generate private/public keys. To generate private/public key set you need to run the following command:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="pl-3 text-syntax-keyword select-none">mirzap@bosnadev:~$<!-- --> </span><span class="whitespace-pre"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">ssh-keygen</span><span class="hl-s"> -t</span><span class="hl-s"> rsa</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>Now you will have an option to name your key pair and set password.</p>
<figure data-size="column" class="not-prose my-10"><span class="block"><button type="button" data-figure-trigger="true" aria-label="Open image: Public Key Encryption" class="block max-w-full cursor-zoom-in text-left outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-background w-fit"><span class="relative block overflow-hidden w-fit max-w-full"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 scale-110 bg-cover bg-center blur-lg transition-opacity duration-300 motion-reduce:transition-none" style="background-image:url(https://bosnadev.com/2015/01/23/&quot;data:image/webp;base64,UklGRoIAAABXRUJQVlA4WAoAAAAQAAAADwAACAAAQUxQSDUAAAABYBzJViLcXW6cWN/8Y+QTQkRMgBVAKxBQbCiVxhDYwj+vcb59wcVgnfPaeBcMEgIBN1gBtABWUDggJgAAADABAJ0BKhAACQADgFolpAADcAD+8r65udLURU3MA1Y2elODYAAA&quot;)"></span><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/cffeee77fb83bbdc/2015-01-public-key-ecryption-640x360.avif 640w, https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/39341fa8109598f9/2015-01-public-key-ecryption-1200x675.avif 1200w" sizes="(min-width: 848px) 768px, (min-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 80px), calc(100vw - 32px)"><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/0e6333f2aff8b4f7/2015-01-public-key-ecryption-640x360.webp 640w, https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/e86aa1360416b5b4/2015-01-public-key-ecryption-1200x675.webp 1200w" sizes="(min-width: 848px) 768px, (min-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 80px), calc(100vw - 32px)"><img src="https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/e86aa1360416b5b4/2015-01-public-key-ecryption-1200x675.webp" alt="Public Key Encryption" width="1200" height="675" decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="relative block h-auto max-w-full"></picture></span></button></span></figure>
<h2 id="transfer-the-public-key-to-the-server">Transfer The Public Key To The Server</h2>
<p>When you have generated private/public key-pair you need to transfer public key to the remote server. This public key will allow you to identify your self to the server. SSH comes with an utility called <em><strong>ssh-copy-id</strong></em> that simply copies content of public key to the server’s ~/.ssh/authorized_keys :</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="pl-3 text-syntax-keyword select-none">mirzap@bosnadev:~$<!-- --> </span><span class="whitespace-pre"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">ssh-copy-id</span><span class="hl-s"> -i</span><span class="hl-s"> .ssh/mirzap.pub</span><span class="hl-s"> user@some_host_or_ip</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>You should have output similar to this:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary absolute top-4 right-3 z-1 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] pl-2">copy</button><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span>Number of key(s) added: 1</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span></span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span>Now try logging into the machine, with:   "ssh '[email protected]_host_or_ip'"</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span>and check to make sure that only the key(s) you wanted were added.</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>If you don’t have <em>ssh-copy-id</em> utility on your system, you can copy content of the public key and add it to the <em>authorized_key</em> by your self.</p>
<h2 id="disable-password-authentication">Disable Password Authentication</h2>
<p>You can now connect to the remote server using a private key you generated, but your system isn’t secure just yet. You need to disable password-based and allow only key-based authentication. You can improve your server security by applying other measures, like changing default port or enabling host-based authentication, but that is not the topic of this article.</p>
<p>To disable password authentication open /etc/ssh/sshd_config and find the following line:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">/etc/ssh/sshd_config</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span>#PasswordAuthentication yes</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>uncomment it, and set to <em>no</em> :</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">/etc/ssh/sshd_config</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span>PasswordAuthentication no</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>Now /etc/ssh/sshd_config should look like this:</p>
<p><img src="https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/019fb787b429f36f/2015-01-disable-pass-auth.webp" alt="Disable Password Authentication" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async">Save and restart SSH server:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">2<!-- --> <!-- -->lines</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="pl-3 text-syntax-keyword select-none">user@secure:~#<!-- --> </span><span class="whitespace-pre"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">/etc/init.d/ssh</span><span class="hl-s"> restart</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre text-[0.8125rem] text-syntax-comment pl-3">[ ok ] Restarting OpenBSD Secure Shell server: sshd.</span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>If you try to connect to the server on the machine without private key, you’ll get this message:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">2<!-- --> <!-- -->lines</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="pl-3 text-syntax-keyword select-none">vagrant@homestead:~$<!-- --> </span><span class="whitespace-pre"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">ssh</span><span class="hl-s"> user@some-host</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre text-[0.8125rem] text-syntax-comment pl-3">Permission denied (publickey).</span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>But on your local machine, where you created private key, authentication should pass without problems:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">3<!-- --> <!-- -->lines</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="pl-3 text-syntax-keyword select-none">mirzap@bosnadev:~$<!-- --> </span><span class="whitespace-pre"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">ssh</span><span class="hl-s"> user@some-host</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre text-[0.8125rem] text-syntax-comment pl-3">Last login: Fri Jan 23 15:24:15 2015 from some-ip</span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre text-[0.8125rem] text-syntax-comment pl-3">user@secure:~#</span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>If you have created password during key generation, you’ll be asked to enter it on each login:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">3<!-- --> <!-- -->lines</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="pl-3 text-syntax-keyword select-none">mirzap@bosnadev:~$<!-- --> </span><span class="whitespace-pre"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">ssh</span><span class="hl-s"> user@some-host</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre text-[0.8125rem] text-syntax-comment pl-3">Enter passphrase for key &#x27;/home/mirzap/.ssh/mirzap_rsa&#x27;:</span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre text-[0.8125rem] text-syntax-comment pl-3">user@secure:~#</span></span></code></pre></div></article></div><div class="hidden pt-32 min-[1152px]:block"><aside class="sticky top-24 max-h-[calc(100vh-7rem)] overflow-y-auto pb-6"><nav aria-label="On this page"><p class="mb-3 border-b pb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-muted-foreground uppercase">On this page</p><ol class="space-y-px"><li><a href="ssh-authentication-keys-instead-passwords#the-idea-of-public-key-cryptography" class="block border-l-2 py-1 pl-3 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary border-transparent text-muted-foreground">The Idea Of Public Key Cryptography</a></li><li><a href="ssh-authentication-keys-instead-passwords#generate-keys" class="block border-l-2 py-1 pl-3 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary border-transparent text-muted-foreground">Generate Keys</a></li><li><a hr